  "title": "Store: rename `NodeInit` → `UpsertNode`, `Identifier` → `NodeIdentifier`; keep children that joined a not-yet-existing parent",
  "body": "## Changelog Entry\n\nNone. This builds on the non-shipping store in #6053, so label it `no-changelog`.\n\n## Description\n\nThis branch sits on top of `feat-new-store` (#6053). It renames two public types. It also fixes the bug that made `goldenStories/autoHasPart.test.ts` fail.\n\n**Bug.** Within one transaction, a child is upserted with `isPartOf: P` while `P` does not exist yet. `P` is then upserted. `P`'s updater receives `undefined`, so it cannot know about the child. `upsert()` still compared the returned `hasPart` with the child it had already recorded for `P`, and dropped the child as a removal.\n\n```ts\ncontroller.edit(transaction => {\n  transaction.upsert('_:m-1', () => ({ '@id': '_:m-1', '@type': new Set(['Message']), isPartOf: new Set([{ '@id': '_:c' }]) }));\n  transaction.upsert('_:c', () => ({ '@id': '_:c', '@type': new Set(['Conversation']) }));\n});\n\nstore.queryByIdentifier('_:c').hasPart; // before: undefined, after: Set { { '@id': '_:m-1' } }\n```\n\n## Design\n\nThe `hasPart` diff now starts from the children actually shown to the updater. For a node that does not exist yet, that is `EMPTY_IDS`. Children that joined through their own `isPartOf` are kept, and anything listed in `hasPart` is added. The `isPartOf` side already works this way: pending parents are always merged into a newly upserted child (`autoIsPartOf.test.ts`).\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> **Review this.** An existing unit test in `Store.test.ts` asserted the opposite: a parent upserted later *replaces* `hasPart`, even with children it never saw. That test now expects them merged (`[m-1, m-2]`).\n>\n> The alternative is to merge only when the updater omits `hasPart`. That passes both tests, but `hasPart` would then behave differently from `isPartOf`.\n\n## Specific Changes\n\n- **Renames**\n   - `NodeInit<T>` → `UpsertNode<T>` (`node/Node.ts`, `Store.ts`, `index.ts`)\n   - `Identifier` → `NodeIdentifier` across `packages/store/src`\n   - `identifierSchema` and the error message strings are unchanged\n- **`Store.ts` `upsert()`**\n   - `getChildIds()` is now stored as `childIdsInGraph` and is still used for the dirty read\n   - `shownChildIds` is `node ? childIdsInGraph : EMPTY_IDS` and drives the `hasPart` diff\n- **`Store.test.ts`**: the \"one side declared\" scenario now expects merge semantics\n- **`private/deepFreeze.objectIs.test.ts`**: fixes an import of `../structure.ts`, which \"Remove structure entry point\" deleted\n- **Not changed, needs a human:** `goldenStories/AGENTS.md` forbids agent edits, so these files still use the old names and fail typecheck until updated:\n   - `goldenStories/upsertedNodeIsDifferentAndFrozen.test.ts` (`NodeInit`, `Identifier`)\n   - `goldenStories/validNodeIdentifier.ts` (`Identifier`)\n\n- [x] I have added tests and executed them locally\n- [x] ~I have added `.changelog/<PR#>-<slug>.md`~\n- [x] ~I have updated documentation~\n\n## Review Checklist\n\n> This section is for contributors to review your work.\n\n- [x] ~Accessibility reviewed (tab order, content readability, alt text, color contrast)~\n- [x] ~Browser and platform compatibilities reviewed~\n- [x] ~CSS styles reviewed (minimal rules, no `z-index`)~\n- [ ] Documents reviewed (docs, samples, live demo)\n- [x] ~Internationalization reviewed (strings, unit formatting)~\n- [x] ~`package.json` and `package-lock.json` reviewed~\n- [x] ~Security reviewed (no data URIs, check for nonce leak)~\n- [ ] Tests reviewed (coverage, legitimacy)",
